From 6045cee15d84ffbe220450d8e8f9462a71dd8cf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:44:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Only pass FFTW's x86 SIMD configure flags on x86 hosts

packaging/build_config.sh passes --enable-sse2 and
--with-incoming-stack-boundary=2 to FFTW's configure unconditionally.
Both are x86-only: on any other architecture FFTW's configure probes the
compiler for -msse2, fails, and aborts with "Need a version of gcc with
-msse2", so build_3rdparty_static_debian.sh cannot build FFTW on
aarch64, riscv64 or any non-x86 Linux host. Keep the two flags for
i?86/x86_64 build machines (which also covers the mingw cross build) and
drop them elsewhere, leaving FFTW's portable scalar codelets.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; upstream publishes no non-x86 Linux wheel, so the gap only shows when the static 3rdparty build runs on another architecture]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 packaging/build_config.sh | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packaging/build_config.sh b/packaging/build_config.sh
index d193130a..25604638 100755
--- a/packaging/build_config.sh
+++ b/packaging/build_config.sh
@@ -205,10 +205,16 @@ FFMPEG_AUDIO_FLAGS_MUXERS="
 # see http://www.fftw.org/install/windows.html
 FFTW_FLAGS="
     --enable-float
+    --with-our-malloc16
+"
+case "$(uname -m)" in
+    i?86|x86_64)
+        FFTW_FLAGS="$FFTW_FLAGS
     --enable-sse2
     --with-incoming-stack-boundary=2
-    --with-our-malloc16
 "
+        ;;
+esac
 
 LIBSAMPLERATE_FLAGS="
     --disable-fftw
